    "label": "Wizard steals the years she has yet to live",
    "truth": "The wizard abducted Valerie because a royal lifespan is bound to an ancient clock of years. He is gradually transferring decades of her future into his own failing body, leaving her apparently healthy but shortening the life she has yet to live. The dragon must discover the theft before its damage becomes irreversible.",
    "cue": "The princess's portraits show subtle unexplained aging while a clock without hands accumulates new marks.",
    "stance": "Grimly practical and increasingly alarmed by gaps in her sense of time; she challenges the wizard's assurances.",
