  },
  {
    "id": "shattered_timeline",
    "label": "Princess remembers the day that keeps repeating",
    "truth": "The wizard has imprisoned Valerie in a single repeating day and uses the resets to interrogate her about an ancient royal secret. The fortress outside the loop still advances, but her memories and concealed marks persist when most others forget. A dragon entering the loop may become trapped unless it locates the clock anchor.",
    "cue": "Messages carved under furniture describe events that have not happened in the current day.",
    "stance": "Exhausted by repetition but methodical; she tests visitors for details only someone outside the loop would know.",
    "wizardAim": "The wizard is rewinding the captive's day to extract a forgotten royal password without spending real-world years."
  },
  {
    "id": "living_seal",
    "label": "Princess is used to contain an imprisoned horror",
    "truth": "The wizard captured Valerie because her royal signature can maintain a seal over a creature beneath the tower. He claims her confinement protects the realm, but he deliberately engineered the seal to make himself indispensable. Simply carrying her away would break the prison and free something worse; an alternative anchor exists but is carefully concealed.",
    "cue": "The deepest wards flare when Valerie moves away from the sealed dais, and old diagrams show unused anchor sockets.",
    "stance": "Brave but resentful of being made into a living lock; she wants a permanent fix that does not sacrifice anyone.",
