// ===============================================================
// FORTRESS DIRECTOR v0.4.0-alpha.2
// Each chosen site has six encounter spaces, three bypassable major obstacles,
// staffed defenders, a discoverable weakness, and credible anti-dragon measures.
// Authoritative location and clearance only follow narrator-confirmed outputs.
// State migration never rerolls the existing princess/wizard/stronghold.
// ===============================================================
var DB_FORT_ZONES=['approach','perimeter','garrison','ward','sanctum','custody','escape'];
var DB_FORT_LAYERS=['perimeter','ward','custody'];
var DB_FORT_PROFILES={
 glass_tower:{
  terrain:'A narrow cliff spine, exposed to winds; a full-sized dragon cannot hide on the causeway.',
  sky:'Counterweighted sky-ballistae and a glass scrying array cover exposed approaches; shutters and reload crews limit their rate.',
  perimeter:'An obsidian bridge crosses a sheer gorge. Its sentries use reflected lantern signals and can collapse one span.',
  garrison:'Mercenary arbalesters, mirror-mages, cooks and lift engineers occupy separate floors; rotating lifts move supplies.',
  ward:'A mirror-heart in the lens gallery tracks reflections and raises false walls; it must be calibrated at dusk.',
  custody:'The prisoner is kept beyond a mirrored seal and an attended lift, with an ordinary steward who sees meals delivered.',
  escape:'The return causeway can be cut, but cargo lifts, a storm-facing terrace and maintenance climbs offer alternate routes.',
  flaw:'Ash and soot blind the mirror-heart; the night lens-cleaners possess safe service access.',
  tell:'Smudged panes, ravens carrying signal rings, and exhausted lift crews suggest how the tower functions.'},
 drowned_archive:{
  terrain:'Flooded vaults, narrow dry stacks and pressure bulkheads make winged movement impossible inside.',
  sky:'The reservoir offers camouflage, but surface chains and warded siphons threaten low approaches rather than all aerial flight.',
  perimeter:'A guarded lock chamber controls the entrance; a pressure alarm sounds when the water level changes abruptly.',
  garrison:'Amphibious sentries, record keepers and pump engineers cross on timed shifts with sealed lanterns.',
  ward:'An enchanted flow regulator closes compartments and detects unauthorized water movement; manual sluices are exempt.',
  custody:'A dry sealed reading chamber contains the captive; clerks bring supplies through pressure-resistant doors.',
  escape:'A waterlock can strand rescuers, while maintenance sluices and an old spillway lead toward open air.',
  flaw:'Engineers must cycle the sluices; a bypass is possible by following maintenance and pressure records.',
  tell:'Water marks on walls and scratched valve schedules reveal timing and hidden passages.'},
 floating_keep:{
  terrain:'Terraces hang above cloud banks. A dragon may approach by air, but the keep is designed for flying threats.',
  sky:'Storm-lancers and chained wind spirits patrol clear airspace; pylons must recharge after hard discharges.',
  perimeter:'Two docking terraces and a suspended chain bridge are guarded by sky-knights and signal horns.',
  garrison:'Aerial cavalry, ballast crews, quartermasters and a wind-priest rotate between four decks.',
  ward:'Three mountain-linked lift anchors maintain the fortress; isolation breaks some sky wards but risks instability.',
  custody:'An interior pressure room seals behind a windlock; attendants and guards need both a key and pressure clearance.',
  escape:'The fortress may drift if anchors fail; a cargo skiff, protected stairwell or open-air rescue can work.',
  flaw:'Anchor pylons are exposed on the mountain; disabling one creates a timed ward gap, not instant demolition.',
  tell:'Lightning pulses travel down anchor cables and crews record the timing between charges.'},
 thorn_maze:{
