var DB_TOWER_STAGE_VARIANTS={
 approach:[
  ['Skywatch Array','Signal crews sweep the available sky lanes in overlapping intervals.','Observe rotation and time a blind interval; negotiate a marked approach; distract a relay crew.','Witnessed flights bring trained defenders rather than instant magical detection.'],
  ['Surveyor’s Stakes','An outer ring of surveyor stakes records unusual movement near the tower.','Map gaps between stakes; move under an escort; disturb a remote stake and cross elsewhere.','A loud disturbance sends a team to verify the actual signal.'],
  ['Scattered Watchposts','A chain of finite watchposts covers terrain routes but leaves supply traffic.','Follow legitimate supplies; win over an isolated scout; disable a signal horn.','A compromised watchpost may fail to report its scheduled check-in.']],
 entry:[
  ['Two-Stage Gate','A portcullis and secondary warded door separate the outside from the first occupied landing.','Breach one mechanism and disable the other; acquire an authorized token; bypass through service architecture.','A violent breach damages routes and alerts nearby guards.'],
  ['Passage of Names','An enchanted registrar records each entry and rejects unfamiliar names.','Find a forgotten guest entry; obtain a registrar’s assistance; interrupt the physical inscription circuit.','A failed false identity creates a report, not universal instant pursuit.'],
  ['Counterweighted Bridge','A massive movable bridge separates the public approach from the tower.','Seize the winch room; secure a maintenance crossing; use plausible dragon flight through an unwarded gap.','Destroying the bridge complicates extraction for non-flying allies.']],
 intelligence:[
  ['Quartermaster’s Circuit','Food, arcane reagents and water pass through monitored servant corridors.','Question a willing worker; trace recurring deliveries; intercept or copy a schedule.','Staff notice shortages and changed routines once their rounds return.'],
  ['Split Command','A castellan and chief wardwright dispute control of one guarded hallway.','Negotiate with one faction; intercept instructions; exploit a routine shift change.','Both factions act on different reports and may misread events.'],
  ['Ledger of Doors','Service doors are listed in a controlled maintenance register.','Read or steal the ledger; persuade a clerk; follow a team repairing a real fault.','Rumors about a stolen ledger spread slowly through the staff.']],
 wardwork:[
  ['Three-Fold Resonator','Three physically separate rune sources reinforce the inner ward.','Identify and disrupt the correct anchor; make the wardwright disconnect a source; exploit a service phase.','Overloading a source can alert staff and endanger the local room.'],
  ['Refraction Gallery','A sequence of reflecting symbols powers a limited detection field.','Reorient a mirror; smear or conceal a lens; use the documented safe maintenance corridor.','A broken lens leaves a real blind zone, not an instant fortress-wide blackout.'],
  ['Bound Oath Seal','The ward admits certain signed oaths and refuses unauthorized entrants.','Locate a valid old oath; negotiate permission; break the anchor that maintains the contract.','An attempted forged oath produces a local response.']],
 sanctum:[
  ['Prepared Spell Circle','The wizard has a fortified casting position and finite prepared resources.','Disrupt an anchor; draw out a costly spell; exploit the wizard’s actual agenda as leverage.','The wizard may withdraw or call known allies, not invent impossible counterspells.'],
  ['Council of Apprentices','Lieutenants guard the study but argue about the wizard’s next order.','Win an ally; intercept messages; create a legitimate split in their ranks.','The wizard might lose time or respond through those who remain loyal.'],
  ['False Sanctum','A convincing copy of the wizard’s laboratory conceals the true command room.','Follow real supply lines; question surviving personnel; identify anomalies in the false workshop.','A wrong guess costs time or supplies but never changes the generated truth.']],
 captive:[
  ['Anchor-Linked Quarters','The captive area has a physical lock and a finite magical restraint with separate maintainers.','Find the real custody key; study the anchor; negotiate release; bypass the ward through a discovered route.','A reckless breach may threaten occupants and require safe extraction planning.'],
  ['Shifted Custody','The custody schedule moves staff between two genuine rooms, while the prisoner is stable at a known location.','Trace kitchen service; interrogate a guard; compare genuine duty lists.','A false lead delays the rescue without relocating the princess arbitrarily.'],
  ['Contract Chamber','A written magical obligation limits access and imposes specific release conditions.','Recover the contract; discover a permitted exception; convince a signatory to release it.','Breaking the text blindly may trigger its known local safeguard.']],
 extraction:[
  ['Cut Return Path','The obvious exit is now contested while secondary paths remain physically present.','Use the established service route; negotiate a ceasefire; fly out through an actually open gap.','Pursuers must travel from their known stations.'],
  ['Cargo and Passenger','A dragon’s route can be too narrow or exposed for a human traveler.','Open a wider service door; carry a willing passenger safely; secure a carriage or temporary shelter.','Poor planning costs time, not automatic recapture.'],
  ['Last Bargain','A surviving defender offers information or a binding truce at the exit.','Accept, reject or expose the offer; use an already-cleared alternate path.','The deal may affect politics after departure but does not reset solved wards.']]
};
// Private plot hooks for all thirty wizard-captor scenarios; Story Cards do not reveal them.
